{
  "abstract": "We study regular extension formulas in an elliptic family of square-product rational Diophantine quintuples parametrized by $V^2=(k^2-2)(k^2+4)$. Of the twenty regular fourth-element expressions from three-subtuples, eight identically repeat existing entries. We prove that none of the twelve remaining expressions extends a nondegenerate family member to a sextuple. Six exclusions follow from rank-zero common-factor obstructions and a Mordell–Weil sieve modulo 47. Two more follow from the complete rational-point classification of $y^2=5(k^2+1)(k^2-2)(k^2+4)$, whose only affine points are $(k,y)=(\\pm2,\\pm20)$. Its two rank-one elliptic quotients support quadratic Chabauty at 13, followed by a primary sieve. The final four expressions require a common quartic factor to represent squareclass one or two. Exact covering descents and elliptic Chabauty over quadratic and quartic number fields show that these conditions occur only at degenerate parameters. The arguments use explicit subgroups and primitive local logarithms without assuming complete Mordell–Weil generators. We also determine the genera of the regular four-subtuple compatibility covers, proving that these separate routes can succeed at only finitely many parameters. At $k=3/2$, full saturation and an exact height certificate also exclude arbitrary sixth entries of logarithmic height at most $3\\,248\\,610$. A portable supplement reconstructs the identities, descents, local series, finite groups and branch counts, including independent implementations of the decisive local calculations. Arbitrary sixth entries and rational septuples remain unresolved.",
